From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-controller: 992 - build topology from assoc on Topology Response

Patch 990 added topology_build_tree_from_assoc and called it every 60s from
cntlr_query_nodes, which correctly writes topology_link. But handle_topology
_response still ran the neighbor-BFS builder (the 988 block), which rebuilds
the tree from the 1905 neighbor graph (first hop only) or leaves it invalid --
and mapc_sync_agent runs right after and reads THAT, so agent.depth (and the
agent_backhaul view / WebUI, which read a.depth) stayed -1 even though
topology_link was correct.

Replace the neighbor-BFS block with the assoc builder so the tree is correct
and valid on every Topology Response, before the DB sync reads depth. Drops the
now-moot 988 gate and the standalone root dance (the assoc builder owns the
root).

Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
---
--- a/src/cntlr_map.c
+++ b/src/cntlr_map.c
@@ -350,7 +350,7 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
-static bool cntlr_is_standalone(struct controller *c)
+static bool __attribute__((unused)) cntlr_is_standalone(struct controller *c)
 {
 	struct node *self = cntlr_find_node(c, c->almacaddr);
 
@@ -800,30 +800,18 @@
 	}
 
 	/* When all topology responses collected, build topology tree. */
-	if (!is_topology_valid(&c->topology)) {
-		bool standalone = cntlr_is_standalone(c);
-
-		/* Gate on agents only. num_agents excludes the colocated controller
-		 * root, but topology_num_devs() includes it, so the old
-		 * num_agents == topology_num_devs() compared two different
-		 * populations and stopped firing once a 2-hop agent joined (root
-		 * present => counts differ), freezing topology_link at the first
-		 * hop. Count agent devs on both sides so the rebuild fires once
-		 * every agent has reported, regardless of the colocated-agent flap. */
-		if (c->num_agents ==
-		    topology_num_agent_devs(&c->topology, c->almacaddr)) {
-			if (standalone) {
-				topology_remove_device(&c->topology, c->almacaddr);
-				build_local_controller_root(c, &c->topology, c->almacaddr);
-			}
-
-			topology_build_tree(c, &c->topology, c->almacaddr);
-
-			/* Send BH policy only when max_node_bh_hops is configured. */
-			if (c->cfg.max_node_bh_hops != 0) {
-				/* Requires valid bBSS netif_iface info */
-				cntlr_send_max_wifi_bh_hops_policy(c);
-			}
+	/* 992: build the backhaul tree from association data (per-node
+	 * upstream_bssid) on every topology update, and do it here so the tree is
+	 * current before the DB sync (mapc_sync_agent) reads depth from it. The
+	 * 1905 neighbor graph structurally misses the wireless bSTA->bBSS hop, so
+	 * the old neighbor-BFS could only ever see the first hop. */
+	if (c->num_agents > 0) {
+		topology_build_tree_from_assoc(c, &c->topology, c->almacaddr);
+
+		/* Send BH policy only when max_node_bh_hops is configured. */
+		if (c->cfg.max_node_bh_hops != 0) {
+			/* Requires valid bBSS netif_iface info */
+			cntlr_send_max_wifi_bh_hops_policy(c);
 		}
 	}
 
